<stringmatch name="vectorabi #1: off, addv takes and returns 8-byte scalars" min="1" max="1">^unsigned long addv\((unsigned long|uint8) a0,(unsigned long|uint8) a1\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #2: off, the VADDPS lanes print as scalar lanes packed into a CONCAT44 (and the default legacy paddd)" min="2" max="2">return CONCAT44\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #3: off, ymm0 is read back out of the widened zmm0" min="1" max="1">SUB6432\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #4: on, the lane run is one intrinsic with __m256 in and out" min="1" max="1">^__m256 addv\(__m256 a0,__m256 a1\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #5: on, addv returns the fused add" min="1" max="1">return _mm256_add_ps\(a0,a1\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #6: on, integer vectors are __m256i" min="1" max="1">^__m256i addi\(__m256i a0,__m256i a1\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #7: on, all three FMA vectors are arguments" min="1" max="1">return _mm256_fmadd_ps\(a0,a1,a2\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #8: on, the merge mask folds into the intrinsic" min="1" max="1">return _mm512_mask_add_ps\(a0,a\d,a\d,a\d\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #9: on, EVEX.z gives the zero-masking form" min="1" max="1">return _mm512_maskz_add_ps\(a\d,a\d,a\d\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #10: on, a VEX.128 add and a legacy SSE addps are __m128 in and out (one VEX, one SSE)" min="2" max="2">^__m128 add128\(__m128 a0,__m128 a1\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #11: the 128-bit float adds fuse to _mm_add_ps" min="2" max="2">return _mm_add_ps\(a0,a1\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #12: legacy SSE paddd keeps its lanes at the default" min="1" max="1">^unsigned long add128i\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #13: lanefuse all fuses SSE2 integer code" min="1" max="1">^__m128i add128i\(__m128i a0,__m128i a1\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vectorabi #14: lanefuse all fuses two-lane doubles" min="1" max="1">return _mm_mul_pd\(a0,a1\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
